From 453c924859828754f11e114ec25e5b812a8b81c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kamal Bura <burakamal13@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:04:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: filogic: add JioRouter AX6000 JIDU6801 to the
 JIDU6J01 target

The JioRouter AX6000 JIDU6801 is a dual-band Wi-Fi 6 router on the
MediaTek MT7986A (Filogic 830) SoC. It is electrically and
device-tree-identical to the boards already covered by
jiorouter_ax6000-jidu6j01, so it is added as a further variant of that
target rather than as a new image and DTS.

Hardware, common to the family:
  - SoC:    MediaTek MT7986A, 4x Cortex-A53 @ 2.0 GHz
  - RAM:    512 MiB DDR4
  - Flash:  256 MiB SPI-NAND (Winbond W25N02KV, MediaTek NMBM)
  - Switch: MediaTek MT7531AE DSA
      * port 0:    1G SGMII/GMII WAN, internal MT7531 PHY
      * ports 1-4: 1G LAN, internal MT7531 PHYs
      * port 6:    2.5G SGMII CPU link to gmac0
  - Wireless: MT7976C DBDC, 4x4 2.4 GHz + 4x4 5 GHz (AX6000)
  - LEDs:   red GPIO 12, green GPIO 13, blue GPIO 14
  - Button: reset GPIO 9
  - USB:    1x USB 3.0 Type-A host
  - UART:   115200 8N1, 3.3 V TTL header

The base MAC is a 6 byte binary value at offset 0 of the MFG partition,
which is what the existing MFG model lookup in 02_network and
11_fix_wifi_mac already falls back to, so no base-files change is needed.

Tested on hardware: kernel boot, the 8 fixed MTD partitions, the 140 MiB
UBI attach, SquashFS root with UBIFS overlay, MT7531 DSA setup, 1G on all
five external ports, 2.5G on the internal CPU link, and both PHYs running
802.11ax at HE40 (2.4 GHz) and HE160 (5 GHz).

Known limitation, and the reason this is not ready to merge: the stock
bootloader on these units keeps bootcmd=mtkboardboot and its boot path
requires a rootfs subimage inside the kernel FIT plus a valid vendor
signature, neither of which an OpenWrt FIT provides. OpenWrt therefore
only boots unattended after the U-Boot environment has been rewritten,
which jiorouter_initial_setup does when the first flash is performed from
the initramfs. A unit flashed by writing the sysupgrade image directly
retains the stock environment and will stop at the U-Boot prompt on the
next cold boot. The flashing procedure and a UART-based workaround for
unattended boot are documented in the project repository; they are being
reworked before this is proposed for merge.

Signed-off-by: Kamal Bura <burakamal13@gmail.com>
---
 target/linux/mediatek/image/filogic.mk | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/linux/mediatek/image/filogic.mk b/target/linux/mediatek/image/filogic.mk
index d07abed..4e45292 100644
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/image/filogic.mk
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/image/filogic.mk
@@ -2346,6 +2346,9 @@ define Device/jiorouter_ax6000-jidu6j01
   DEVICE_ALT3_VENDOR := JioRouter
   DEVICE_ALT3_MODEL := AX6000
   DEVICE_ALT3_VARIANT := JIDU6701
+  DEVICE_ALT4_VENDOR := JioRouter
+  DEVICE_ALT4_MODEL := AX6000
+  DEVICE_ALT4_VARIANT := JIDU6801
   DEVICE_DTS := mt7986a-jiorouter-ax6000-jidu6j01
   DEVICE_DTS_DIR := ../dts
   DEVICE_PACKAGES := kmod-usb3 kmod-mt7915e kmod-mt7986-firmware mt7986-wo-firmware
